# CUSUM calibration (seeds 100+, not used for reporting)

h = 1.25 × the largest CUSUM value seen in any clean experiment (clean runs plus the pre-change part of change runs), so no clean calibration experiment would flag.

| drift | h | changes caught on the contaminated experiment | mean change-time error (s) |
|---|---|---|---|
| 0.5 | 68.3 | 9/24 | 0.037 |
| 1.0 | 51.9 | 10/24 | 0.058 |
| 2.0 | 22.9 | 11/24 | 0.095 |
| 3.0 | 8.3 | 12/24 | 0.179 |
| 4.0 | 3.3 | 13/24 | 0.180 |
| 5.0 | 1.6 | 13/24 | 0.187 |

Chosen: drift = 4.0, h = 3.3 (most changes caught; ties go to the smaller drift).

